# ── Separated repositories ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These live in their own repos and are checked out here as sibling directories,
# so the relative `file:` dependencies between them keep resolving (npm resolves
# by filesystem path, not repo boundary):
#   idl-wallet-v2/              → github.com/janskor-cz/idl-wallet
#   identus-document-service/   → github.com/janskor-cz/identus-document-service
# This repo keeps the rest of the infrastructure: CA, company-admin-portal,
# packages/ (shared DIDComm libraries, consumed via file:../packages/…),
# the frozen idl-wallet v1, and the docs.
idl-wallet-v2/
identus-document-service/

# idl-wallet-kotlin/ → github.com/janskor-cz/idl-wallet-kotlin — a Gradle project, not npm, so no
# file: dependency to preserve; checked out here purely so this repo's kotlin-port/ spec and
# idl-wallet-v2 porting source are easy to read side by side. Built/run on a different machine.
idl-wallet-kotlin/

# Runtime data (regenerated by the services; not source)
company-admin-portal/data/
certification-authority/data/chat-messages.json
certification-authority/data/photo-dids.json
certification-authority/data/user-connection-mappings.json
certification-authority/data/soft-deleted-connections.json
idl-wallet/data/wallet-registry.json
# Live in-person verification codes — short-lived secrets, never commit
certification-authority/data/credential-verification-codes.json
# Ad-hoc data backups
**/*.bak-*

